class.description:
Write one function that takes a [NetwBitStream]. Call it with a [method writer] to write, a [method reader] to read, or a [method measurer] to count the bits without writing.
[codeblock]
func describe(s: NetwBitStream, row: Dictionary) -> Dictionary:
    row.hp = s.bits(row.get("hp", 0), 12)
    row.name = s.string(row.get("name", ""))
    s.align_verify()
    return row

var out := NetwBitStream.writer()
describe(out, {"hp": 87, "name": "hero"})
var bytes := out.to_bytes()

var back := NetwBitStream.reader(bytes)
var row := describe(back, {})
if not back.ok() or back.bits_remaining() != 0:
    push_error("rejected")
[/codeblock]
After a read fails, every call does nothing, so check [method ok] once at the end. Reject the data when [method bits_remaining] is not [code]0[/code]. End every payload with [method align_verify].
